{title: In Charge of the Outside Work}
{subtitle: Ezra 8:33; Nehemiah 8:7; 11:16; Ezra 10:23; Nehemiah 12:44–45}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] [F/A] | [Gm7] [Eb] | [Bb] [F/A] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
On the fourth [Bb]day they [F/A]weighed the [Gm7]silver
Gold and [Eb]vessels in the house of our [Fsus4]God
[F]Into the [Bb]hands of the [F/A]priests they [Gm7]went
With the Le[Eb]vites standing close [Fsus4]by
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[F]Jo[Gm7]saphat son of [Eb]Jeshua was [Bb]there
Noadiah [Gm7]son of Binnui [Eb][Fsus4]too
[F]Weighing [Gm7]out what was brought [Eb]from exile
[Bb/D]Recording [Gm7]all that the people [Fsus4][F]gave
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In charge of [Bb]the outside [F]work
Of the [Gm7]house of God he [Eb]stood
Keeping the [Bb]charge of his [F]God
As the [Eb]singers and [Fsus4]gatekeepers [Bb]did [F/A][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]The Levites ex[F/A]plained [Gm7]the Law
While [Eb]the people remained in their pla[Fsus4]ces
[F]Jes[Bb]hua Bani [F/A]Sherebi[Gm7]ah
Jamin Ak[Eb]kub Shabbethai Ho[Fsus4]diah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[F]Maaseiah [Gm7]Kelita Aza[Eb]riah [Bb]
Joza[Gm7]bad Ha[Eb]nan and Pelaiah [Fsus4]
[F]They [Gm7]made the words [Eb]plain and clear
[Bb/D]To the assem[Gm7]bly gathered [Fsus4]there
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]In charge of [Bb]the outside [F]work
Of the [Gm7]house of God he [Eb]stood
Keeping the [Bb]charge of his [F]God
As the [Eb]singers and [Fsus4]gatekeepers [Bb]did
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Shabbethai and [F]Jozabad [Bb]stood
[Eb]Two heads [F]of the Le[Bb]vites
[Eb]Managing the dai[F]ly service
Of the [Gm]temple life they [Eb]led
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
According to the command
Of [Fsus4]David and Solo[F]mon
They kept the [Gm]charge of [F/A]purity
[Eb]In the house of our [Bb][F/A][Gm]God [Eb][Bb][F/A][Eb]
{end_of_verse}
